-- Page — a hosted public page (routable, publishable, composed of typed
-- blocks). Six fields: a refined-String slug (kebab pattern), a String
-- name, an EntityRef<"entity_definition"> type (the entity that this
-- page submits / displays), a list of typed Blocks (single-case for
-- now: a form block), a PageConfig record for brand / logo / thank-you /
-- redirect, and a Boolean published flag.
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity is registered from the Fenel directives below.
--
-- Phase 3e of the system-entities sweep — see
-- workstreams/ts-elimination/briefs/phase-3e-page-entity-discriminator.md.
-- The flagship test of the new `@discriminator "<name>"` directive
-- grammar: Page.blocks is `List PageBlock` where PageBlock is a
-- single-case `$variant` with a custom `"type"` discriminator slot (the
-- pre-3e behavior, preserved bug-compatibly so persisted page rows that
-- read `b.type === "form"` keep working — see api/src/routes/pages.ts).
--
-- The PageBlock ctor is named `form` (lowercase) to match the
-- discriminator value persisted in existing page rows. ValidateUnion
-- reads `obj[disc]` against the variant case-names, so the case-name must
-- equal the persisted string verbatim. `PageBlock` (the type head) stays
-- uppercase per the parser's `isUpperCase(head)` rule for type-decls;
-- only the ctor name is lowercase.
--
-- PageBlock was a directive-less local `Block`, never registered, so
-- `page.blocks` named whichever registered `Block` a registry held —
-- Notion's, which required an `id` (modules-as-values Phase 5 per-owner
-- type identity, S1). It is now its own registered system type.
--
-- The `@discriminator "type"` directive also blocks the single-ctor-
-- with-named-fields → `$record` collapse in fenel-module.ts's
-- `typeDefToPureFenelType` — without it, `PageBlock = form typeRef: …
-- functionId: … submitLabel: …` would lower to a `$record` because
-- all fields are named (see Phase 3e brief Watch-out §6). The
-- directive forces the variant shape so the discriminator slot
-- remains load-bearing as future block-types (text / image / video /
-- etc.) land.
--
-- PageSlug reuses the canonical `str:case:kebab` named set. It denotes the
-- same `[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*` language as the retired inline regex while
-- remaining bootstrap-safe: loading a source module no longer tries to enter
-- the Fenel regex runtime while that runtime's registry is still being built.
--
-- The config sub-record is authored inline (not as a named PageConfig
-- atom) so the `config.redirectUrl → "Redirect URL"` per-field label
-- selector descends through `$record.fields` directly and is resolved to the
-- leaf UUID by the field-representation kernel after identity collection.
-- UrlStr is the cross-entity refined-String atom from proxy_link.fenel;
-- reusing it from there avoids a duplicate refined-String declaration.

@entity
@label "Page Slug"
@description "String matching the kebab-case slug pattern ([a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*)"
PageSlug = String | value ∈ str:case:kebab

@entity
@label "Page Block"
@description "A typed block of a hosted page; today a form block (the type, the submitting function and the submit label)"
@discriminator "type"
PageBlock = form typeRef: EntityRef<"entity_definition"> functionId: EntityRef<"function"> submitLabel: String

@entity
@codeName "page"
@label "Page"
@description "A hosted public page — routable, publishable, composed of typed blocks"
@icon "globe"
@fieldLabel "config.redirectUrl" "Redirect URL"
Page = Page slug: PageSlug name: String type: EntityRef<"entity_definition"> blocks: List PageBlock config: { brandColor: String, logo: String, thankYouMessage: String, redirectUrl: UrlStr } published: Boolean
